ID: B3-Ch01a-Dance
TEXT:

"Want me to do a little dance too, while I'm at it?" I ask, turning to face him.

"Actually, not a bad idea," Daren says with a dry grin. "Try that dwarven jig where you hop on one boot with your hands locked behind your head. I'll tell you when you've spun enough."

"My dwarven dance tutor skipped that chapter," I say. "Now, are you going to explain what we're doing, or am I pacing circles until dawn?"

"Right, right," Daren says, catching himself with an embarrassed clearing of his throat. "I should have explained."

He pauses, looking slightly self-conscious under the starlight.

